{"uid":"6bfab9b13f989d0d","name":"test_the_un_reopen_edge_is_refused_for_an_operator_or_steer_claim_never_a_free_claim","fullName":"tests.test_amendment_status_applier#test_the_un_reopen_edge_is_refused_for_an_operator_or_steer_claim_never_a_free_claim","historyId":"17281398080ec290e4d2e92753a7e504","time":{"start":1791919557631,"stop":1791919557636,"duration":5},"description":"Cure-01-05-2 (PRD requirement B.3/B.4, F05, #221) corrects this\n    node's own original claim -- that an OPERATOR ruling or a STEER update\n    could drive the un-reopen edge directly through `apply_task_status_\n    change`, before `_reconcile_pre_cure_heads` (B.4, task 008) existed to\n    be the edge's real caller. F05's own `cured_when` is explicit: \"the\n    declared un-reopen edge is available only for an ENGINE reconciliation\n    of a genuinely reopened record to its persisted prior status\" --\n    ruling 1 itself never carved out an operator or a steer exception, and\n    either one moving a never-reopened task straight to a terminal status\n    is exactly the same widening as a worker's. `apply_task_status_change`\n    only ever passes `allow_un_reopen_restore=True` for its own `source=\n    \"cure-reconciliation\"` branch (`state.py`), so every other source is\n    refused -- checked here for both real production callers,\n    `apply_amendment_status_rulings`'s own `source=\"operator\"` and\n    `steer_task_update`'s own `source=\"steer\"`, kept as ONE parametrized\n    node (zero fast-tier headroom -- no new collected item over the two\n    this replaces) rather than a sibling per source.\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p>Cure-01-05-2 (PRD requirement B.3/B.4, F05, #221) corrects this<br />\nnode's own original claim -- that an OPERATOR ruling or a STEER update<br />\ncould drive the un-reopen edge directly through <code>apply_task_status_ change</code>, before <code>_reconcile_pre_cure_heads</code> (B.4, task 008) existed to<br />\nbe the edge's real caller. F05's own <code>cured_when</code> is explicit: &quot;the<br />\ndeclared un-reopen edge is available only for an ENGINE reconciliation<br />\nof a genuinely reopened record to its persisted prior status&quot; --<br />\nruling 1 itself never carved out an operator or a steer exception, and<br />\neither one moving a never-reopened task straight to a terminal status<br />\nis exactly the same widening as a worker's. <code>apply_task_status_change</code><br />\nonly ever passes <code>allow_un_reopen_restore=True</code> for its own <code>source= &quot;cure-reconciliation&quot;</code> branch (<code>state.py</code>), so every other source is<br />\nrefused -- checked here for both real production callers,<br />\n<code>apply_amendment_status_rulings</code>'s own <code>source=&quot;operator&quot;</code> and<br />\n<code>steer_task_update</code>'s own <code>source=&quot;steer&quot;</code>, kept as ONE parametrized<br />\nnode (zero fast-tier headroom -- no new collected item over the two<br />\nthis replaces) rather than a sibling per source.</p>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"monkeypatch","time":{"start":1791919557600,"stop":1791919557600,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_home_in_process","time":{"start":1791919557601,"stop":1791919557611,"duration":10},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_scrub_notifier_env_in_process","time":{"start":1791919557611,"stop":1791919557621,"duration":10},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name